From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 20:21:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] boot: use real autoboot seconds on BM201

The vendor Amlogic branch advances each displayed autoboot unit after 100 ms.
The configured three-second prompt therefore accepts input for only about
300 ms, which is too short to react after the HDMI prompt becomes visible.

Keep that vendor behavior for other boards and use U-Boot's normal 1000 ms
unit on BM201, where the HDMI and USB console is deliberately interactive.
---
diff --git a/bl33/v2023/common/autoboot.c b/bl33/v2023/common/autoboot.c
index a3eb64db110a7236ed33f82fa04f331713bea2ed..ff6f8ad1ccc450afcdc0874d65a8e4436275cad1 100644
--- a/bl33/v2023/common/autoboot.c
+++ b/bl33/v2023/common/autoboot.c
@@ -406,7 +406,7 @@ static int abortboot_single_key(int bootdelay)
 					menukey = key;
 				break;
 			}
-#ifdef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MODIFY
+#if defined(CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MODIFY) && !defined(CONFIG_S7D_BM201)
 			udelay(10000);
 		} while (!abort && get_timer(ts) < 100);
 #else
